1
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:20,726
Where are the secretaries?

2
00:00:20,727 --> 00:00:23,367
(Where are the secretaries?)

3
00:00:24,407 --> 00:00:27,807
(I can't ask my manager to do something like this.)

4
00:00:28,177 --> 00:00:30,877
(But I can ask my secretary.)

5
00:00:31,077 --> 00:00:34,377
(Don't secretaries usually handle more discreet matters?)

6
00:00:37,687 --> 00:00:39,346
(A secretary is someone who stays by your side...)

7
00:00:39,347 --> 00:00:40,886
(and shares even your most closely guarded secrets.)

8
00:00:40,887 --> 00:00:42,917
A secretary is...

9
00:00:43,057 --> 00:00:44,956
How many people in Korea have their own secretaries?

10
00:00:44,957 --> 00:00:46,057
Let's be real.

11
00:00:46,257 --> 00:00:49,826
Unless you're a CEO, you don't get to have your own secretary.

12
00:00:49,827 --> 00:00:51,543
(They've returned with the dignity of true secretaries.)

13
00:00:51,567 --> 00:00:53,167
That's why you can't get used to it.

14
00:00:55,037 --> 00:00:56,897
(My gosh)

15
00:00:57,637 --> 00:00:58,937
You startled me.

16
00:00:58,967 --> 00:01:00,767
It's hot. Stay away from me.

17
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:02,336
(Sticking together)

18
00:01:02,337 --> 00:01:03,937
Hey. I'm only sticking with you...

19
00:01:04,477 --> 00:01:06,676
- because the producer told me to.
- It's hot.

20
00:01:06,677 --> 00:01:08,976
(Season 2 opens with an adorable shot of the 2 together.)

21
00:01:08,977 --> 00:01:10,577
Do you like your partner?

22
00:01:11,347 --> 00:01:12,487
What if I don't?

23
00:01:12,747 --> 00:01:13,847
Will you replace him?

24
00:01:14,147 --> 00:01:15,557
(Dimples coming out)

25
00:01:15,857 --> 00:01:17,116
(He senses his job is in danger.)

26
00:01:17,117 --> 00:01:18,156
So...

27
00:01:18,157 --> 00:01:19,327
What do you think?

28
00:01:19,557 --> 00:01:20,856
Me?

29
00:01:20,857 --> 00:01:22,457
(Suddenly polite)

30
00:01:22,597 --> 00:01:24,766
- Why did you suddenly get polite?
- No.

31
00:01:24,767 --> 00:01:26,027
- Well...
- Why?

32
00:01:26,467 --> 00:01:28,636
I've done everything on this show.

33
00:01:28,637 --> 00:01:30,466
I drank sundae soup in a car.

34
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:31,936
(I drank sundae soup in a car.)

35
00:01:31,937 --> 00:01:33,206
I put contact lenses in someone's eyes.

36
00:01:33,207 --> 00:01:34,483
(I put contact lenses in someone's eyes.)

37
00:01:34,507 --> 00:01:35,936
(My Star is satisfied.)

38
00:01:35,937 --> 00:01:37,307
I filmed a challenge.

39
00:01:37,977 --> 00:01:39,746
I hosted the pre-concert segment.

40
00:01:39,747 --> 00:01:40,853
(I hosted the pre-concert segment.)

41
00:01:40,877 --> 00:01:44,317
(I gave acting advice.)

42
00:01:44,517 --> 00:01:48,056
(I put nail tips on someone's fingernails.)

43
00:01:48,057 --> 00:01:49,457
I even sang.

44
00:01:50,217 --> 00:01:52,817
If you're curious, why don't you come and experience it yourself?

45
00:01:53,057 --> 00:01:54,356
I, Lee Seo Jin,

46
00:01:54,357 --> 00:01:55,427
will do anything for you.

47
00:01:57,097 --> 00:01:58,866
Can you say your last line again?

48
00:01:58,867 --> 00:02:01,266
Say, "If you're curious, come to our show as My Star."

49
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:03,537
That's basically like begging.

50
00:02:04,167 --> 00:02:05,636
Gosh, that's annoying.

51
00:02:05,637 --> 00:02:06,906
That's the most annoying thing in the world.

52
00:02:06,907 --> 00:02:08,007
(It hurts his pride.)

53
00:02:08,507 --> 00:02:10,337
But you're determined, aren't you?

54
00:02:10,907 --> 00:02:11,947
"Determined?"

55
00:02:12,207 --> 00:02:13,977
I said I'd take care of them.

56
00:02:14,447 --> 00:02:15,817
Isn't that enough?

57
00:02:16,777 --> 00:02:18,987
So just come and see it yourself.

58
00:02:19,587 --> 00:02:21,027
If you're curious, come on the show.

59
00:02:21,157 --> 00:02:22,157
If you aren't, just forget it.

60
00:02:22,158 --> 00:02:24,727
(My Genie Secretary warmly welcomes My Stars.)

61
00:02:24,987 --> 00:02:25,987
(Clearing his throat)

62
00:02:25,988 --> 00:02:29,457
I heard some unsettling rumors recently.

63
00:02:29,597 --> 00:02:31,326
There's been a lot of talk...

64
00:02:31,327 --> 00:02:33,567
that either Kwang Soo or Kwang Hee might be coming.

65
00:02:33,597 --> 00:02:36,466
Who else could handle that fussy young master?

66
00:02:36,467 --> 00:02:37,597
That's me.

67
00:02:37,707 --> 00:02:40,667
No one else can do it.

68
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:43,707
He's only doing so well...

69
00:02:43,937 --> 00:02:45,683
because I've been there supporting him all along.

70
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:48,346
Seo Jin was...

71
00:02:48,347 --> 00:02:49,347
(Laughing)

72
00:02:49,547 --> 00:02:53,117
Seo Jin was... No. Seo Jin...

73
00:02:54,247 --> 00:02:55,287
Seo Jin...

74
00:02:57,417 --> 00:02:59,357
Hey, close the door.

75
00:02:59,957 --> 00:03:03,257
(He even makes the young master laugh.)

76
00:03:03,457 --> 00:03:05,097
Genie will do anything for you.

77
00:03:05,267 --> 00:03:06,897
Do you think you can do this without me?

78
00:03:07,067 --> 00:03:10,437
I'll do anything for you!

79
00:03:10,597 --> 00:03:13,036
(Grander)

80
00:03:13,037 --> 00:03:15,537
(More meticulous)

81
00:03:16,037 --> 00:03:17,876
(Secretaries are ready to pour their hearts into the job.)

82
00:03:17,877 --> 00:03:19,947
I'm so tired.

83
00:03:20,807 --> 00:03:23,246
(If My Star wants something, )

84
00:03:23,247 --> 00:03:25,387
(they'll do anything to make it happen.)

85
00:03:25,717 --> 00:03:27,856
(The one and only pair of Genies...)

86
00:03:27,857 --> 00:03:29,756
(who can make your wishes come true)

87
00:03:29,757 --> 00:03:31,556
Genie will do anything for you. My Genie Secretary.

88
00:03:31,557 --> 00:03:34,497
(Genie Will Do Anything for You, My Genie Secretary)

89
00:03:35,457 --> 00:03:38,927
(The secretaries who will do anything for My Star have come...)

90
00:03:39,327 --> 00:03:42,637
(to the hottest festival in Korea right now.)

91
00:03:42,897 --> 00:03:44,707
(Waterbomb Festival 2026)

92
00:03:44,907 --> 00:03:47,807
(The combination of water and music will beat the heat.)

93
00:03:48,177 --> 00:03:50,353
(The 2026 Waterbomb Festival drew a cumulative audience of 830,000.)

94
00:03:50,377 --> 00:03:53,017
(As of 2025, the festival was held in 13 cities around the world.)

95
00:03:53,507 --> 00:03:57,517
(Right in the heart of youth, )

96
00:03:58,387 --> 00:04:03,957
(where streams of water rain down on artists as they take the stage)

97
00:04:06,927 --> 00:04:08,556
I'm a top-tier marksman.

98
00:04:08,557 --> 00:04:10,838
(A 60-year-old secretary came to the Waterbomb Festival.)

99
00:04:11,767 --> 00:04:13,397
What's the concept for today's outfit?

100
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:15,897
The Waterbomb Festival.

101
00:04:18,567 --> 00:04:19,806
(A very simple outfit of the day)

102
00:04:19,807 --> 00:04:21,576
It's "water."

103
00:04:21,577 --> 00:04:23,737
(Wearing a knit shirt under the scorching sun)

104
00:04:23,937 --> 00:04:25,446
But what does "bomb" mean?

105
00:04:25,447 --> 00:04:27,777
(What does "bomb" mean in "Waterbomb?")

106
00:04:27,847 --> 00:04:29,447
What do you think Seo Jin will wear?

107
00:04:30,217 --> 00:04:33,087
I think he might wear shorts.

108
00:04:34,087 --> 00:04:36,257
Today, he'll be wearing shorts...

109
00:04:37,057 --> 00:04:41,427
a short-sleeved shirt,

110
00:04:42,227 --> 00:04:44,157
a thin necklace,

111
00:04:45,597 --> 00:04:50,437
and two thin bracelets on his right wrist.

112
00:04:51,367 --> 00:04:52,436
- Here he is.
- Yes.

113
00:04:52,437 --> 00:04:54,407
(Seo Genie came at the perfect time.)

114
00:04:54,977 --> 00:04:57,477
(Loading his water gun)

115
00:04:58,547 --> 00:04:59,577
(Sliding)

116
00:05:01,317 --> 00:05:02,517
Gosh.

117
00:05:08,017 --> 00:05:09,317
My prediction was right.

118
00:05:10,417 --> 00:05:12,933
(A thin necklace and bracelet, a short-sleeved shirt, and shorts)

119
00:05:12,957 --> 00:05:15,827
(He correctly guessed what Seo Jin would wear to the festival.)

120
00:05:16,197 --> 00:05:18,667
(He fearlessly sprays him with a water gun.)

121
00:05:19,597 --> 00:05:20,667
Stop it.

122
00:05:22,997 --> 00:05:24,707
(Scared)

123
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:27,936
(The lovebugs are overflowing with affection from the start.)

124
00:05:27,937 --> 00:05:29,507
(Glancing)

125
00:05:30,037 --> 00:05:31,447
You're wearing shorts.

126
00:05:32,107 --> 00:05:33,547
You can't wear shorts when you work.

127
00:05:33,577 --> 00:05:35,577
Do you think your outfit is okay?

128
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:39,417
Hey. This is for the Waterbomb Festival. The blue moon.

129
00:05:41,087 --> 00:05:43,163
What does it have to do with the Waterbomb Festival?

130
00:05:43,187 --> 00:05:44,256
(Barking)

131
00:05:44,257 --> 00:05:46,287
- Hey.
- What? Even the dog is barking.

132
00:05:47,087 --> 00:05:48,157
That darn dog...

133
00:05:49,157 --> 00:05:50,227
- Hey.
- Yes?

134
00:05:50,327 --> 00:05:52,597
- "Water" means water.
- Yes.

135
00:05:53,067 --> 00:05:54,327
What does "bomb" mean?

136
00:05:54,837 --> 00:05:55,897
Bomb.

137
00:05:56,537 --> 00:05:58,907
You're a former Army sergeant. How do you not know that?

138
00:05:59,937 --> 00:06:02,476
(So "bomb" doesn't mean night?)

139
00:06:02,477 --> 00:06:04,707
So "bomb" means bomb?

140
00:06:05,707 --> 00:06:08,047
Everyone is holding a water gun.

141
00:06:08,317 --> 00:06:09,446
- Hey.
- I think...

142
00:06:09,447 --> 00:06:10,877
this is a restricted military area.

143
00:06:11,847 --> 00:06:14,546
- Is that so?
- Everyone has a gun.

144
00:06:14,547 --> 00:06:16,716
- Well...
- What?

145
00:06:16,717 --> 00:06:19,186
I'll show off my bayonet-fighting skills today.

146
00:06:19,187 --> 00:06:21,086
- You brought a gun too.
- I brought my gun.

147
00:06:21,087 --> 00:06:23,957
I prepared it for BIBI.

148
00:06:24,457 --> 00:06:26,467
Did you look into her?

149
00:06:26,727 --> 00:06:28,797
Yesterday, I watched YouTube...

150
00:06:28,997 --> 00:06:30,637
- all night.
- Okay.

151
00:06:31,737 --> 00:06:33,467
- Let me tell you about BIBI.
- Go on.

152
00:06:33,837 --> 00:06:36,807
Her most widely known song is "Yeon Yang Gang."

153
00:06:37,237 --> 00:06:39,447
- It's "Bam Yang Gang." - "Bam Yang Gang."

154
00:06:39,807 --> 00:06:41,976
Are you hungry again?

155
00:06:41,977 --> 00:06:43,677
- Have you not eaten?
- No, I haven't.

156
00:06:44,117 --> 00:06:46,186
- My gosh.
- I had a bit of chicken porridge.

157
00:06:46,187 --> 00:06:47,747
"Yeon Yang Gang?" What was that?

158
00:06:53,987 --> 00:06:55,356
(Making her 5th appearance at the Waterbomb Festival this year, )

159
00:06:55,357 --> 00:06:57,027
(she's the original Waterbomb Queen.)

160
00:06:57,297 --> 00:07:02,837
(From "Bam Yang Gang," which took Korea by storm, )

161
00:07:04,807 --> 00:07:09,507
(to "BIBI Vengeance," which has racked up over 100 million views)

162
00:07:09,937 --> 00:07:11,776
("10th on Billboard's '20 Best K-pop Songs of 2024'")

163
00:07:11,777 --> 00:07:13,217
("From Number 1 Korea to Billboard")

164
00:07:13,477 --> 00:07:18,516
(She's a global star who made it into the Billboard charts.)

165
00:07:18,517 --> 00:07:20,317
Hello, I'm Kim Hyeong Seo.

166
00:07:20,917 --> 00:07:23,416
(She won the Excellence Award at the SBS Drama Awards...)

167
00:07:23,417 --> 00:07:24,977
(for her role in "The Fiery Priest 2.")

168
00:07:25,257 --> 00:07:27,587
(Today's My Star transcends genres, from music to acting.)

169
00:07:29,297 --> 00:07:30,456
Hello.

170
00:07:30,457 --> 00:07:31,767
(My Star in the meantime)

171
00:07:32,267 --> 00:07:33,727
Hi.

172
00:07:34,227 --> 00:07:35,267
That was nice.

173
00:07:36,637 --> 00:07:41,377
(She's already busy before the show even starts.)

174
00:07:42,077 --> 00:07:47,107
(See you soon, secretaries.)

175
00:07:47,307 --> 00:07:49,176
- Let's go.
- Yes.

176
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:51,346
- The artist will be arriving soon.
- Yes. Let's go.

177
00:07:51,347 --> 00:07:52,707
(They hurry over to meet My Star.)

178
00:07:52,747 --> 00:07:53,817
Where should we go?

179
00:07:54,887 --> 00:07:56,363
We're supposed to get through all those people?

180
00:07:56,387 --> 00:07:57,617
There's only one way.

181
00:07:58,457 --> 00:08:01,287
(Crowded)

182
00:08:01,927 --> 00:08:05,767
(The entrance is packed with young people from all over the country.)

183
00:08:07,197 --> 00:08:08,336
(There are just too many people.)

184
00:08:08,337 --> 00:08:09,767
Kwang Kyu, bring the gun.

185
00:08:11,267 --> 00:08:12,536
Yes, sir.

186
00:08:12,537 --> 00:08:13,966
(The first schedule: Meet the Waterbomb Queen)

187
00:08:13,967 --> 00:08:15,107
Load your gun.

188
00:08:15,337 --> 00:08:16,736
- It's loaded.
- What?

189
00:08:16,737 --> 00:08:17,837
It's loaded.

190
00:08:23,517 --> 00:08:26,917
- Oh, my gosh.
- My goodness.

191
00:08:27,547 --> 00:08:28,957
It's My Genie Secretary.

192
00:08:30,257 --> 00:08:34,687
(People recognize them as they approach the entrance.)

193
00:08:35,227 --> 00:08:37,797
(Shy and happy)

194
00:08:38,627 --> 00:08:40,026
- Oh, my.
- It's cold.

195
00:08:40,027 --> 00:08:42,367
- Hi! How are you?
- I know you!

196
00:08:42,737 --> 00:08:44,907
(Even an international attendee recognized him.)

197
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:46,166
- Oh, my.
- Hi.

198
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:47,807
- I know you!
- How are you?

199
00:08:48,277 --> 00:08:49,937
Thank you, and you?

200
00:08:51,577 --> 00:08:53,807
I can speak English today.

201
00:08:54,677 --> 00:08:56,016
You just said, "Fine, thank you."

202
00:08:56,017 --> 00:08:58,177
(The energy of the young crowd gets them all excited.)

203
00:08:58,487 --> 00:09:00,187
- It's hot.
- It's hot.

204
00:09:01,587 --> 00:09:02,756
A nice, cold draft beer would be...

205
00:09:02,757 --> 00:09:04,077
(I want a nice, cold draft beer.)

206
00:09:04,387 --> 00:09:05,456
(It felt like 42°C on the day of filming.)

207
00:09:05,457 --> 00:09:08,127
(Safey Advisory: Extreme heat is expected to continue.)

208
00:09:08,827 --> 00:09:10,197
It's so hot.

209
00:09:14,467 --> 00:09:16,067
(A woman in a crop top)

210
00:09:16,737 --> 00:09:18,637
(Half-naked men)

211
00:09:19,307 --> 00:09:21,937
I guess everyone is wearing swimwear here.

212
00:09:25,607 --> 00:09:28,847
(Swimwear everywhere)

213
00:09:28,917 --> 00:09:30,993
(A special Waterbomb Festival dress code made for the summer heat)

214
00:09:31,017 --> 00:09:34,887
(Some people are shirtless.)

215
00:09:35,957 --> 00:09:40,057
(Bundled up)

216
00:09:41,127 --> 00:09:44,897
(Wait. That's what we're supposed to wear here?)

217
00:09:45,467 --> 00:09:47,297
I looked around.

218
00:09:47,797 --> 00:09:50,037
No one was dressed like us.

219
00:09:50,537 --> 00:09:51,937
I was shocked.

220
00:09:52,507 --> 00:09:55,177
Everyone was shirtless, but I couldn't take off my shirt.

221
00:09:55,807 --> 00:09:57,137
I used to be fit.

222
00:09:58,447 --> 00:10:00,176
It's not unusual...

223
00:10:00,177 --> 00:10:02,677
to walk around in swimwear in the States.

224
00:10:03,417 --> 00:10:06,187
I guess Korea is being more open-minded too.

225
00:10:06,887 --> 00:10:09,987
The culture seems to have changed a lot.

226
00:10:10,887 --> 00:10:13,557
(They're strolling around, pretending everything is fine.)

227
00:10:15,297 --> 00:10:19,967
(But you can tell he's flustered by looking at his pouty lips.)

228
00:10:23,467 --> 00:10:26,107
(The water cannons fire.)

229
00:10:26,867 --> 00:10:30,607
(The blast of water sends their excitement through the roof.)

230
00:10:31,037 --> 00:10:33,507
(Startled)

231
00:10:33,847 --> 00:10:38,387
(They even fire the water cannons?)

232
00:10:41,187 --> 00:10:42,387
"What's going on?"

233
00:10:42,757 --> 00:10:46,157
"Is this how young people play these days?"

234
00:10:46,627 --> 00:10:49,507
When we were little, all we did was play with water using plastic bowls.

235
00:10:50,157 --> 00:10:51,826
It was surprising.

236
00:10:51,827 --> 00:10:53,967
I didn't know it was that big of a festival.

237
00:10:55,167 --> 00:10:58,437
(We didn't play like this.)

238
00:11:01,067 --> 00:11:04,037
(What's that?)

239
00:11:07,377 --> 00:11:09,717
(A whole new discovery)

240
00:11:11,687 --> 00:11:15,987
(There's a giant water gun that people can actually fire.)

241
00:11:16,557 --> 00:11:20,027
(Interested)

242
00:11:22,597 --> 00:11:26,027
(He goes straight to it.)

243
00:11:30,737 --> 00:11:31,837
So you can fire this?

244
00:11:34,067 --> 00:11:35,977
(A blast of water)

245
00:11:36,437 --> 00:11:38,406
(He got soaked trying out the new technology.)

246
00:11:38,407 --> 00:11:40,177
(This is fun.)

247
00:11:41,107 --> 00:11:43,417
(Going back)

248
00:11:44,447 --> 00:11:45,816
(One more time)

249
00:11:45,817 --> 00:11:46,887
(Cheering)

250
00:11:50,557 --> 00:11:54,997
(He quickly adapts to the new technology.)

251
00:11:55,397 --> 00:11:58,727
(Satisfied)

252
00:11:59,697 --> 00:12:01,667
(Should I try firing the water gun too?)

253
00:12:01,767 --> 00:12:04,197
(Kwang Kyu is firing the gun.)

254
00:12:05,037 --> 00:12:08,007
(Let's play together, secretaries.)

255
00:12:09,537 --> 00:12:13,747
(Young people's culture is pretty fascinating.)

256
00:12:14,007 --> 00:12:15,617
Did someone shoot a water gun at us?

257
00:12:16,577 --> 00:12:18,077
- What?
- Did someone shoot us?

258
00:12:18,547 --> 00:12:19,586
It's the water you shot.

259
00:12:19,587 --> 00:12:21,347
- It came back to me?
- Because of the wind.

260
00:12:25,887 --> 00:12:28,356
(Gosh, I'm completely soaked.)

261
00:12:28,357 --> 00:12:29,557
Is this the waiting room?

262
00:12:32,797 --> 00:12:35,596
(Meanwhile, today's My Star...)

263
00:12:35,597 --> 00:12:37,967
(is waiting for the secretaries.)

264
00:12:38,337 --> 00:12:43,737
(My Star, BIBI)

265
00:12:44,177 --> 00:12:45,546
- BIBI is...
- Oh, gosh.

266
00:12:45,547 --> 00:12:48,147
(Lee Gyu Rim, BIBI's manager)

267
00:12:49,677 --> 00:12:52,346
(Looking around)

268
00:12:52,347 --> 00:12:54,346
- Why is it so hot in here?
- Did you turn on the fan?

269
00:12:54,347 --> 00:12:55,417
What's this place for?

270
00:12:56,587 --> 00:13:01,327
(They're going to meet My Star now.)

271
00:13:01,927 --> 00:13:07,097
(5 seconds before meeting My Star)

272
00:13:08,197 --> 00:13:09,537
Hello.

273
00:13:10,897 --> 00:13:11,907
Hello.

274
00:13:12,207 --> 00:13:14,707
Is that BIBI? No, she's not. Or is she?

275
00:13:15,507 --> 00:13:16,577
- Is that BIBI?
- BIBI.

276
00:13:18,237 --> 00:13:22,347
(They didn't recognize her because...)

277
00:13:22,477 --> 00:13:25,216
(of the backlighting and their aging eyes.)

278
00:13:25,217 --> 00:13:27,186
(Blurry vision)

279
00:13:27,187 --> 00:13:28,416
- She is.
- She is?

280
00:13:28,417 --> 00:13:29,586
Hello.

281
00:13:29,587 --> 00:13:32,186
It's BIBI.

282
00:13:32,187 --> 00:13:33,757
- Is she?
- Yes.

283
00:13:34,057 --> 00:13:35,896
Is that BIBI? Is that so?

284
00:13:35,897 --> 00:13:38,327
(He messed up. He didn't recognize My Star.)

285
00:13:39,597 --> 00:13:41,066
(Oh, hello.)

286
00:13:41,067 --> 00:13:42,236
(Oh, My Star.)

287
00:13:42,237 --> 00:13:44,866
It was the backlighting. We couldn't really see your face.

288
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:46,137
- Is that so?
- Yes.

289
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:48,066
- Hello.
- Hello.

290
00:13:48,067 --> 00:13:49,136
(They warmly greet each other, but...)

291
00:13:49,137 --> 00:13:50,536
- Hello.
- Hello.

292
00:13:50,537 --> 00:13:51,606
(Could it be because things got off on the wrong foot?)

293
00:13:51,607 --> 00:13:53,527
- It's nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you too.

294
00:13:53,677 --> 00:13:54,677
(Cheering)

295
00:13:54,678 --> 00:13:55,816
(It looks delicious.)

296
00:13:55,817 --> 00:13:57,416
(Don't eat something like that!)

297
00:13:57,417 --> 00:13:58,947
(Why are you telling me what to do?)

298
00:13:59,247 --> 00:14:02,417
(Strict Secretary 1 doesn't cut her any slack.)

299
00:14:02,617 --> 00:14:04,787
(Where is Kwang Kyu?)

300
00:14:04,987 --> 00:14:07,787
(Oh, it's someone else's waiting room.)

301
00:14:07,987 --> 00:14:09,556
(Gosh, this is frustrating!)

302
00:14:09,557 --> 00:14:11,057
(You make me so tired.)

303
00:14:11,767 --> 00:14:14,267
(Absent-minded Secretary 2 is in for a serious scolding.)

304
00:14:14,767 --> 00:14:19,107
(A tear-soaked day for My Star and the middle-aged secretaries)

305
00:14:19,807 --> 00:14:21,207
Why were you sitting here?

306
00:14:21,437 --> 00:14:22,806
It was cold inside.

307
00:14:22,807 --> 00:14:24,877
- It was cold?
- It was cold over there.

308
00:14:25,607 --> 00:14:26,847
It was cold.

309
00:14:26,947 --> 00:14:28,447
We're so hot.

310
00:14:29,177 --> 00:14:31,016
- It was cold for me.
- Then...

311
00:14:31,017 --> 00:14:32,517
- shall we sit here?
- Yes.

312
00:14:33,587 --> 00:14:34,746
How about this table?

313
00:14:34,747 --> 00:14:36,616
(It's hot for them, but they sit outside for My Star.)

314
00:14:36,617 --> 00:14:38,157
- Take a seat.
- Okay.

315
00:14:38,457 --> 00:14:39,926
You're very tall.

316
00:14:39,927 --> 00:14:41,686
- Yes. People often tell me...
- Right?

317
00:14:41,687 --> 00:14:43,367
- I'm taller than they expected.
- Oh, my.

318
00:14:43,727 --> 00:14:45,796
- You're quite tall.
- Are you 168cm?

319
00:14:45,797 --> 00:14:46,996
Yes, I'm 168cm.

320
00:14:46,997 --> 00:14:48,637
How did you know?

321
00:14:48,997 --> 00:14:50,467
(A big reaction)

322
00:14:50,537 --> 00:14:52,066
I got it right.

323
00:14:52,067 --> 00:14:54,437
(Her reaction makes him feel proud.)

324
00:14:54,837 --> 00:14:55,906
He's happy.

325
00:14:55,907 --> 00:14:58,337
(My Star has big reactions.)

326
00:14:58,777 --> 00:15:02,176
(They took a seat, but...)

327
00:15:02,177 --> 00:15:04,417
(Looking around awkwardly)

328
00:15:05,077 --> 00:15:08,287
(Fumbling awkwardly)

329
00:15:09,187 --> 00:15:12,127
- Then...
- It feels different.

330
00:15:12,257 --> 00:15:13,257
What feels different?

331
00:15:14,027 --> 00:15:16,526
It's different from how you looked in the drama with all that makeup.

332
00:15:16,527 --> 00:15:18,356
(In "The Fiery Priest 2")

333
00:15:18,357 --> 00:15:19,996
- Right.
- I watched the drama yesterday.

334
00:15:19,997 --> 00:15:21,427
- I see.
- Yes.

335
00:15:22,167 --> 00:15:24,267
(Actually...)

336
00:15:24,467 --> 00:15:28,407
(From hard-hitting action...)

337
00:15:29,037 --> 00:15:32,177
(and heart-wrenching tearjerkers...)

338
00:15:32,877 --> 00:15:37,417
(to hilarious comedy where she even gets to smack other actors, )

339
00:15:37,947 --> 00:15:41,347
(she's a versatile actress who can do it all.)

340
00:15:41,747 --> 00:15:43,516
You look different from how you did in the drama.

341
00:15:43,517 --> 00:15:44,556
(He tries to break the ice by talking about her acting.)

342
00:15:44,557 --> 00:15:48,386
I'm a big fan of the show produced by Na Yeong Seok.

343
00:15:48,387 --> 00:15:49,626
You've met him, haven't you?

344
00:15:49,627 --> 00:15:51,097
- I've seen your shows.
- Yes.

345
00:15:51,457 --> 00:15:53,296
So it feels like I know you so well.

346
00:15:53,297 --> 00:15:56,197
I've seen both of you so much on TV shows.

347
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:59,637
(My Star and the secretaries can relate to each other a lot.)

348
00:16:00,707 --> 00:16:03,336
What's this? This is so uncomfortable.

349
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:05,806
Is this a cushion designed for hemorrhoids or something?

350
00:16:05,807 --> 00:16:07,546
What's this? This is so uncomfortable.

351
00:16:07,547 --> 00:16:09,976
(My Star feels uncomfortable because of the chair.)

352
00:16:09,977 --> 00:16:12,616
- Turn slightly to the side.
- Like this?

353
00:16:12,617 --> 00:16:14,287
(A useful tip)

354
00:16:14,547 --> 00:16:16,486
It'd be better if you turned the chair slightly.

355
00:16:16,487 --> 00:16:17,516
- Turn the chair?
- Like this.

356
00:16:17,517 --> 00:16:19,326
- Should I turn the chair?
- Yes.

357
00:16:19,327 --> 00:16:20,656
- You can rest your arm like that.
- How is it?

358
00:16:20,657 --> 00:16:21,856
- How is it?
- It's nice.

359
00:16:21,857 --> 00:16:23,757
- I knew it.
- I can rest my arm like this too.

360
00:16:24,557 --> 00:16:25,626
I did it.

361
00:16:25,627 --> 00:16:27,787
(I think I'll do a great job looking after her today.)

362
00:16:27,827 --> 00:16:30,236
(His thoughtful attentiveness has won her over.)

363
00:16:30,237 --> 00:16:32,336
First off, this is my manager.

364
00:16:32,337 --> 00:16:34,136
Nice to meet you. I'm Lee Gyu Rim.

365
00:16:34,137 --> 00:16:35,477
Hello.

366
00:16:35,707 --> 00:16:37,336
This is a transition document.

367
00:16:37,337 --> 00:16:38,857
(Handing over the transition document)

368
00:16:39,107 --> 00:16:40,546
(He hasn't had a handover in 7 months.)

369
00:16:40,547 --> 00:16:42,646
We're not going anywhere else today.

370
00:16:42,647 --> 00:16:44,676
(My Star's schedule)

371
00:16:44,677 --> 00:16:45,916
(2:35pm, An eyewear brand booth event)

372
00:16:45,917 --> 00:16:47,646
(2:55pm, A shampoo brand booth event)

373
00:16:47,647 --> 00:16:50,957
(There are many events and photoshoots as well.)

374
00:16:51,357 --> 00:16:54,286
(It's packed with various events.)

375
00:16:54,287 --> 00:16:57,197
You've been to the Waterbomb Festival a lot, right?

376
00:16:57,727 --> 00:17:00,766
One, two, three, four...

377
00:17:00,767 --> 00:17:01,796
This is my fourth time.

378
00:17:01,797 --> 00:17:02,937
- Fourth?
- Yes.

379
00:17:03,497 --> 00:17:05,266
(Since 2022)

380
00:17:05,267 --> 00:17:09,676
(My Star's performed at the Waterbomb Festival every year.)

381
00:17:09,677 --> 00:17:12,577
I've been coming here every year.

382
00:17:13,447 --> 00:17:14,853
How many songs are you going to sing today?

383
00:17:14,877 --> 00:17:17,116
- Sorry? Maybe 7?
- How many songs? 4?

384
00:17:17,117 --> 00:17:18,786
- Seven.
- Seven?

385
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:19,817
Yes.

386
00:17:20,117 --> 00:17:23,186
(Seven songs on a hot day like this?)

387
00:17:23,187 --> 00:17:24,747
Can you do that while getting drenched?

388
00:17:26,527 --> 00:17:28,456
Your face looks so much smaller in person than it does on screen.

389
00:17:28,457 --> 00:17:29,696
Thank you.

390
00:17:29,697 --> 00:17:31,856
Are you going to sing "The Weekend" today?

391
00:17:31,857 --> 00:17:33,796
- "The Weekend?" - That's the first song.

392
00:17:33,797 --> 00:17:34,826
What's "The Weekend?"

393
00:17:34,827 --> 00:17:37,267
How high did that song chart on Billboard?

394
00:17:37,667 --> 00:17:40,067
- It peaked at number 29...
- Okay.

395
00:17:40,767 --> 00:17:41,976
- on the Radio Songs.
- In...

396
00:17:41,977 --> 00:17:43,536
- the States?
- In the States.

397
00:17:43,537 --> 00:17:44,537
In the American radio chart?

398
00:17:44,538 --> 00:17:46,147
- Were the lyrics in English?
- Yes.

399
00:17:46,677 --> 00:17:49,046
Is your most-viewed music video...

400
00:17:49,047 --> 00:17:50,976
"BIBI Vengeance," with over 100 million views?

401
00:17:50,977 --> 00:17:52,346
Right. It's "BIBI Vengeance."

402
00:17:52,347 --> 00:17:53,893
Does it have more views than "Bam Yang Gang?"

403
00:17:53,917 --> 00:17:55,756
- Right.
- In the other countries.

404
00:17:55,757 --> 00:17:56,956
In Korea, "Bam Yang Gang" was a massive hit.

405
00:17:56,957 --> 00:17:58,416
But "BIBI Vengeance..."

406
00:17:58,417 --> 00:17:59,786
- was my biggest international hit.
- Are there any swear words...

407
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,157
in the lyrics?

408
00:18:01,287 --> 00:18:02,856
The Korean title is "Bad X." Is "X" a B-word?

409
00:18:02,857 --> 00:18:04,727
- What is "X?" - It is a B-word.

410
00:18:05,257 --> 00:18:06,426
(Like this?)

411
00:18:06,427 --> 00:18:07,666
That's right.

412
00:18:07,667 --> 00:18:08,667
(He proudly sang along to the lyrics he memorized.)

413
00:18:08,668 --> 00:18:09,943
I listened to the song yesterday.

414
00:18:09,967 --> 00:18:13,536
Actually, out of all the songs I'm going to perform today,

415
00:18:13,537 --> 00:18:16,036
"Bam Yang Gang" is pretty much the only song you can play on TV.

416
00:18:16,037 --> 00:18:17,983
You're the only one who didn't know the song. He didn't know the song.

417
00:18:18,007 --> 00:18:19,953
- He didn't know "Bam Yang Gang?" - He didn't know the song.

418
00:18:19,977 --> 00:18:22,316
(He didn't know "Bam Yang Gang?")

419
00:18:22,317 --> 00:18:24,016
I knew it.

420
00:18:24,017 --> 00:18:25,747
But he didn't know.

421
00:18:26,147 --> 00:18:28,086
You're the only one who didn't know the song. He didn't know the song.

422
00:18:28,087 --> 00:18:29,717
(Why would you say that?)

423
00:18:30,057 --> 00:18:31,086
(He heard the song for the first time while learning about her.)

424
00:18:31,087 --> 00:18:32,226
(Looking at her nervously)

425
00:18:32,227 --> 00:18:34,126
My gosh. He didn't know the song.

426
00:18:34,127 --> 00:18:35,573
Did you deliberately try to avoid listening to it?

427
00:18:35,597 --> 00:18:36,856
"Oh, it's 'Bam Yang Gang!' I'm not going to listen to it!"

428
00:18:36,857 --> 00:18:38,256
It was played so much. I can't believe you've never heard it...

429
00:18:38,257 --> 00:18:39,426
unless you deliberately tried to avoid it.

430
00:18:39,427 --> 00:18:40,727
That's not it.

431
00:18:41,297 --> 00:18:43,796
I don't know many songs.

432
00:18:43,797 --> 00:18:45,567
I don't know many artists or songs.

433
00:18:46,007 --> 00:18:47,867
Don't you listen to the radio while driving?

434
00:18:48,777 --> 00:18:50,077
I don't listen to Korean music.

435
00:18:51,037 --> 00:18:52,076
(You're doomed.)

436
00:18:52,077 --> 00:18:53,807
What?

437
00:18:53,977 --> 00:18:56,176
(His excuse only made things worse.)

438
00:18:56,177 --> 00:18:59,616
- He's quite annoying.
- He's annoying.

439
00:18:59,617 --> 00:19:00,937
I definitely got that impression.

440
00:19:00,987 --> 00:19:03,516
(Annoying)

441
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:04,617
I mean...

442
00:19:04,987 --> 00:19:06,557
when I was a student,

443
00:19:07,257 --> 00:19:09,657
they only played English songs on the radio.

444
00:19:10,197 --> 00:19:11,397
They didn't play Korean music.

445
00:19:13,327 --> 00:19:15,936
- What are you talking about?
- But...

446
00:19:15,937 --> 00:19:17,496
- it's 2026 now.
- So...

447
00:19:17,497 --> 00:19:19,266
I'm stuck in the past.

448
00:19:19,267 --> 00:19:20,606
You're stuck in the past?

449
00:19:20,607 --> 00:19:22,176
- Right.
- Some people are like that.

450
00:19:22,177 --> 00:19:24,006
I don't listen to modern English songs.

451
00:19:24,007 --> 00:19:26,806
I listen to old ones.

452
00:19:26,807 --> 00:19:28,176
I don't know new songs.

453
00:19:28,177 --> 00:19:29,617
Like what?

454
00:19:29,677 --> 00:19:30,876
Old ones.

455
00:19:30,877 --> 00:19:32,046
(My Star is trying to relate to him.)

456
00:19:32,047 --> 00:19:33,846
We're from the same generation, but I only listen to Korean music.

457
00:19:33,847 --> 00:19:36,116
("Reality," the soundtrack from the movie "La Boum")

458
00:19:36,117 --> 00:19:37,616
Yes. Do you know this song?

459
00:19:37,617 --> 00:19:38,986
(The middle-aged man is happy.)

460
00:19:38,987 --> 00:19:41,556
It goes like this, right?

461
00:19:41,557 --> 00:19:42,997
- Sophie Marceau?
- Yes.

462
00:19:43,997 --> 00:19:45,567
You kind of remind me of her.

463
00:19:47,027 --> 00:19:48,567
You kind of look like her.

464
00:19:48,937 --> 00:19:50,066
I don't think so.

465
00:19:50,067 --> 00:19:51,596
- No. I see the resemblance.
- That's...

466
00:19:51,597 --> 00:19:52,736
No.

467
00:19:52,737 --> 00:19:53,766
(Annoying)

468
00:19:53,767 --> 00:19:54,866
Who do you think she looks like then?

469
00:19:54,867 --> 00:19:56,537
(He ruined my mood.)

470
00:19:57,307 --> 00:19:58,776
(He needs to do something to leave a better impression.)

471
00:19:58,777 --> 00:19:59,947
Talk wisely.

472
00:20:02,647 --> 00:20:04,487
If I had to compare you to a Western singer...

473
00:20:05,947 --> 00:20:06,947
Talk wisely.

474
00:20:07,087 --> 00:20:08,967
I'd say you give off a Christina Aguilera vibe.

475
00:20:10,017 --> 00:20:12,757
- I love her.
- You give off a Christina vibe.

476
00:20:13,427 --> 00:20:15,386
(Not annoying)

477
00:20:15,387 --> 00:20:16,727
This is fun.

478
00:20:17,757 --> 00:20:19,027
Why am I having so much fun?

479
00:20:19,227 --> 00:20:21,796
- Is that so?
- Yes.

480
00:20:21,797 --> 00:20:23,536
Aren't you from Busan?

481
00:20:23,537 --> 00:20:24,737
I'm from Changwon.

482
00:20:24,867 --> 00:20:27,066
- I'm sorry.
- You messed up.

483
00:20:27,067 --> 00:20:29,636
But I read online that you're from Busan.

484
00:20:29,637 --> 00:20:31,236
I was born in Busan...

485
00:20:31,237 --> 00:20:33,146
- and went to college there.
- You went to college there.

486
00:20:33,147 --> 00:20:36,246
My parents are from Busan.

487
00:20:36,247 --> 00:20:37,916
My family has been from Busan for generations.

488
00:20:37,917 --> 00:20:40,447
I'm so happy to meet you. We're from the same city.

489
00:20:40,747 --> 00:20:42,386
- I'll speak to you casually now.
- Sure.

490
00:20:42,387 --> 00:20:43,756
- Gosh.
- I don't mind.

491
00:20:43,757 --> 00:20:46,026
If there's anything you want us to do, don't hesitate to ask.

492
00:20:46,027 --> 00:20:47,327
- Okay.
- Today...

493
00:20:47,527 --> 00:20:51,497
Even if you had a daughter, she'd still be older than her.

494
00:20:51,957 --> 00:20:55,366
- Right.
- Do you have a son?

495
00:20:55,367 --> 00:20:56,996
- What?
- Do you have a son?

496
00:20:56,997 --> 00:20:59,767
(He's 58 and single.)

497
00:21:00,007 --> 00:21:02,207
No, he doesn't.

498
00:21:02,677 --> 00:21:04,576
He's not married.

499
00:21:04,577 --> 00:21:06,707
But he's old. I bet he's older than your father.

500
00:21:06,947 --> 00:21:08,746
My father was born in 1968.

501
00:21:08,747 --> 00:21:10,393
So I was right. He's one year older than your father.

502
00:21:10,417 --> 00:21:12,317
- I told you.
- My goodness.

503
00:21:12,687 --> 00:21:13,946
Oh, my gosh.

504
00:21:13,947 --> 00:21:16,056
You look a lot younger than your age.

505
00:21:16,057 --> 00:21:18,116
You haven't changed at all.

506
00:21:18,117 --> 00:21:19,933
(Would she be okay with being looked after by an old man?)

507
00:21:19,957 --> 00:21:21,986
(He checks her schedule again.)

508
00:21:21,987 --> 00:21:23,726
- There are some events.
- Yes.

509
00:21:23,727 --> 00:21:26,296
Before the show,

510
00:21:26,297 --> 00:21:28,026
I'm going to attend some events.

511
00:21:28,027 --> 00:21:29,096
- Two events.
- Yes.

512
00:21:29,097 --> 00:21:30,496
But there'll be people...

513
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:33,967
on the way to the booth.

514
00:21:34,237 --> 00:21:35,466
You're so pretty!

515
00:21:35,467 --> 00:21:40,707
(The original Waterbomb Queen draws a crowd wherever she goes.)

516
00:21:40,847 --> 00:21:45,247
(They'll act as her bodyguards for safety.)

517
00:21:45,517 --> 00:21:47,686
Please take good care of her.

518
00:21:47,687 --> 00:21:50,486
It'd be great if you could distract people.

519
00:21:50,487 --> 00:21:52,116
There's an eyewear brand booth event?

