("She Got It" by BIBI)

1575
01:05:56,349 --> 01:05:58,418
(Trying to look calm)

1576
01:05:58,419 --> 01:06:00,419
(Staring at nothing)

1577
01:06:04,319 --> 01:06:06,389
(The water cannon goes off.)

1578
01:06:09,859 --> 01:06:13,999
(Giving off rainy season old-couple vibes)

1579
01:06:14,729 --> 01:06:18,399
(Meanwhile, the Waterbombers enjoy it with their whole bodies.)

1580
01:06:19,739 --> 01:06:24,109
(The hot performances come one after the other without a break.)

1581
01:06:26,809 --> 01:06:30,279
BIBI is a born artist. Yes, she is.

1582
01:06:30,609 --> 01:06:33,749
She looked nervous, but when she got on stage,

1583
01:06:34,179 --> 01:06:36,589
you couldn't tell at all.

1584
01:06:36,719 --> 01:06:38,619
"As expected of a pro."

1585
01:06:38,789 --> 01:06:40,789
"She's the real deal."

1586
01:06:42,159 --> 01:06:44,929
(Singing her debut song, "BINU," as the last song)

1587
01:06:45,259 --> 01:06:48,529
(Engaging with the audience with passion until the very end)

1588
01:06:49,129 --> 01:06:52,199
I have a philosophy when it comes to my performances.

1589
01:06:52,569 --> 01:06:54,099
"Give them their money's worth!"

1590
01:06:54,339 --> 01:06:58,339
"Make sure everyone who paid to be here has an amazing time!"

1591
01:07:00,409 --> 01:07:01,678
(BIBI killed this year's Waterbomb!)

1592
01:07:01,679 --> 01:07:03,078
(I hope Korea has more unique artists like her.)

1593
01:07:03,079 --> 01:07:05,519
(BIBI must know she's charming. She was the Waterbomb Queen!)

1594
01:07:07,079 --> 01:07:09,088
Thank you. This was BIBI!

1595
01:07:09,089 --> 01:07:11,129
(The Waterbomb Divinity proved herself once again.)

1596
01:07:13,889 --> 01:07:14,929
I love you!

1597
01:07:15,189 --> 01:07:16,429
See you again!

1598
01:07:18,029 --> 01:07:19,228
Oh, my.

1599
01:07:19,229 --> 01:07:21,359
(At last, a sigh of relief.)

1600
01:07:21,599 --> 01:07:23,128
- Good work.
- Good job, everyone.

1601
01:07:23,129 --> 01:07:24,369
- Good job.
- Look at her.

1602
01:07:27,299 --> 01:07:31,679
(My Star has a hard time even standing up properly.)

1603
01:07:33,639 --> 01:07:38,179
(Her whole body is soaked in sweat and water.)

1604
01:07:41,649 --> 01:07:42,719
It's over!

1605
01:07:43,219 --> 01:07:44,319
I feel so relieved!

1606
01:07:45,359 --> 01:07:46,718
It's over!

1607
01:07:46,719 --> 01:07:49,859
(Seo Genie takes care of My Star without a word.)

1608
01:07:51,729 --> 01:07:53,329
You can finally eat as much as you want!

1609
01:07:53,599 --> 01:07:55,069
I'm going to grab some grub!

1610
01:07:57,229 --> 01:08:00,639
How does it end so quickly when I prepared it for months?

1611
01:08:02,009 --> 01:08:03,569
Good luck!

1612
01:08:04,069 --> 01:08:05,109
Great job.

1613
01:08:09,079 --> 01:08:10,239
Didn't it end really quickly?

1614
01:08:10,649 --> 01:08:11,749
It did.

1615
01:08:12,979 --> 01:08:16,149
You said you were nervous, but it didn't seem like it at all.

1616
01:08:16,519 --> 01:08:18,818
(She's finally laughing.)

1617
01:08:18,819 --> 01:08:20,818
You looked so relaxed singing the first song.

1618
01:08:20,819 --> 01:08:23,728
- Really?
- Yes, you looked super relaxed.

1619
01:08:23,729 --> 01:08:25,599
(Cheering her up with endless compliments)

1620
01:08:26,229 --> 01:08:30,799
When I pour my everything out for 30 minutes...

1621
01:08:30,929 --> 01:08:33,039
and see people sing along,

1622
01:08:33,669 --> 01:08:35,439
do you know how exciting it is?

1623
01:08:36,209 --> 01:08:38,608
I know because I released two albums.

1624
01:08:38,609 --> 01:08:39,839
Right, you did.

1625
01:08:40,109 --> 01:08:42,048
Everyone sings along to Bam Yang Gang.

1626
01:08:42,049 --> 01:08:44,249
Yes, and seeing them sing along was...

1627
01:08:44,449 --> 01:08:46,219
And that many people too.

1628
01:08:46,349 --> 01:08:48,689
I spotted many foreigners today.

1629
01:08:48,819 --> 01:08:49,819
Weren't half the audience...

1630
01:08:49,819 --> 01:08:50,819
- foreigners?
- Right?

1631
01:08:50,820 --> 01:08:52,780
(A rewarding performance after all the hard work)

1632
01:08:52,989 --> 01:08:55,229
- Well done.
- Good job.

1633
01:08:56,159 --> 01:08:57,228
- You worked hard.
- Be careful.

1634
01:08:57,229 --> 01:08:59,269
- We're leaving.
- Dig into lots of delicious food.

1635
01:09:00,399 --> 01:09:02,468
It's over!

1636
01:09:02,469 --> 01:09:03,769
It's over.

1637
01:09:04,129 --> 01:09:05,809
Were you already munching on Homerun Ball?

1638
01:09:07,039 --> 01:09:08,609
- Yes.
- Really.

1639
01:09:09,569 --> 01:09:12,579
You should fuel up with some good food later, not with snacks.

1640
01:09:12,679 --> 01:09:14,949
I won't miss out on the good food either.

1641
01:09:16,349 --> 01:09:17,409
By any chance...

1642
01:09:18,149 --> 01:09:19,279
What? What is it?

1643
01:09:19,549 --> 01:09:21,518
Can you order food for me?

1644
01:09:21,519 --> 01:09:22,548
Sure, what kind?

1645
01:09:22,549 --> 01:09:24,118
(Genie will order anything.)

1646
01:09:24,119 --> 01:09:25,719
We can get delivery there.

1647
01:09:27,359 --> 01:09:28,429
Hold on.

1648
01:09:28,929 --> 01:09:30,265
Do I have to change the address first?

1649
01:09:30,289 --> 01:09:32,298
- I'll do it.
- Give me a second.

1650
01:09:32,299 --> 01:09:33,859
(Unable to trust him)

1651
01:09:33,959 --> 01:09:35,728
What's the address? What was the name?

1652
01:09:35,729 --> 01:09:37,199
Nakasu.

1653
01:09:37,329 --> 01:09:38,539
- Na?
- Na.

1654
01:09:38,839 --> 01:09:40,838
Na as in N, A.

1655
01:09:40,839 --> 01:09:42,838
(Even entering the address isn't easy.)

1656
01:09:42,839 --> 01:09:43,968
Nakasu.

1657
01:09:43,969 --> 01:09:45,509
(Anxious that he might get it wrong)

1658
01:09:45,909 --> 01:09:48,039
Let me check if it's the right place.

1659
01:09:48,649 --> 01:09:49,749
Please.

1660
01:09:50,349 --> 01:09:51,379
Good.

1661
01:09:51,779 --> 01:09:53,579
(Relieved)

1662
01:09:54,119 --> 01:09:55,959
Korean beef intestines and spicy chicken feet.

1663
01:09:56,219 --> 01:09:57,388
With noodles?

1664
01:09:57,389 --> 01:09:59,818
Gosh, it looks good.

1665
01:09:59,819 --> 01:10:01,458
- I...
- Crunchy cubed radish?

1666
01:10:01,459 --> 01:10:02,788
- Yes.
- Or wrap it radish?

1667
01:10:02,789 --> 01:10:04,229
Crunchy cubed radish.

1668
01:10:05,459 --> 01:10:06,659
Is there nothing to add?

1669
01:10:06,929 --> 01:10:07,959
No.

1670
01:10:09,329 --> 01:10:10,668
All right, we're off.

1671
01:10:10,669 --> 01:10:13,439
(6:10pm, heading to the wrap-up party place)

1672
01:10:15,669 --> 01:10:18,008
- Hold on, Kwang Kyu.
- Okay.

1673
01:10:18,009 --> 01:10:20,108
- Hold on, Kwang Kyu.
- What is it?

1674
01:10:20,109 --> 01:10:22,408
My fans are waiting outside.

1675
01:10:22,409 --> 01:10:23,409
Give me a minute.

1676
01:10:23,779 --> 01:10:26,749
(The fans are waiting for My Star on her way home.)

1677
01:10:27,449 --> 01:10:28,548
Stop.

1678
01:10:28,549 --> 01:10:29,589
(Growing impatient)

1679
01:10:29,989 --> 01:10:31,789
(The window isn't rolling down.)

1680
01:10:32,189 --> 01:10:34,459
- Kwang Kyu, roll down the window.
- Okay.

1681
01:10:34,519 --> 01:10:35,828
(Rolling down the window)

1682
01:10:35,829 --> 01:10:36,929
The window.

1683
01:10:37,729 --> 01:10:39,859
- Stop.
- Okay, stop.

1684
01:10:40,529 --> 01:10:41,698
How was it today?

1685
01:10:41,699 --> 01:10:44,229
- You're so pretty!
- Oh, my gosh.

1686
01:10:44,569 --> 01:10:46,069
What a princess!

1687
01:10:46,239 --> 01:10:47,369
I love you all.

1688
01:10:47,769 --> 01:10:49,309
Thanks for coming.

1689
01:10:49,509 --> 01:10:50,569
Bye.

1690
01:10:51,609 --> 01:10:53,708
(Feeling proud of My Star's popularity)

1691
01:10:53,709 --> 01:10:54,709
You were good.

1692
01:10:54,710 --> 01:10:56,830
- How was the new choreography?
- The choreography...

1693
01:10:57,179 --> 01:10:58,679
Was the remix okay?

1694
01:11:01,649 --> 01:11:04,719
(My Star's fans spotted the secretaries.)

1695
01:11:05,119 --> 01:11:06,818
What does your dad do?

1696
01:11:06,819 --> 01:11:08,658
- Thank you. Bye!
- Bye!

1697
01:11:08,659 --> 01:11:10,589
(A fan service for My Star's fans)

1698
01:11:11,829 --> 01:11:13,859
(Bye!)

1699
01:11:14,129 --> 01:11:16,369
- Thank you!
- What does your dad do?

1700
01:11:17,129 --> 01:11:19,299
(Excited with BIBI)

1701
01:11:19,999 --> 01:11:21,279
You talk to your fans like that?

1702
01:11:21,839 --> 01:11:23,669
I'm close with those fans.

1703
01:11:24,409 --> 01:11:25,638
They're a year older than me.

1704
01:11:25,639 --> 01:11:26,879
- Really?
- Yes.

1705
01:11:28,039 --> 01:11:29,308
Shall we get going?

1706
01:11:29,309 --> 01:11:32,619
(Leaving the venue and heading to My Star's regular hangout)

1707
01:11:34,349 --> 01:11:36,389
I prepared it for months,

1708
01:11:36,689 --> 01:11:38,689
but the 30 minutes passed by in a flash.

1709
01:11:39,519 --> 01:11:40,919
One song got you relaxed, right?

1710
01:11:41,589 --> 01:11:43,058
- Yes.
- Usually...

1711
01:11:43,059 --> 01:11:45,798
Yes, and I thought I should get through it.

1712
01:11:45,799 --> 01:11:48,629
Before you get on stage to perform,

1713
01:11:48,869 --> 01:11:50,729
- you get all nervous.
- True.

1714
01:11:51,069 --> 01:11:53,539
But after one song...

1715
01:11:54,269 --> 01:11:55,309
I totally agree.

1716
01:11:55,669 --> 01:11:58,779
Because of the adrenaline rush, I didn't know I got hurt.

1717
01:11:59,579 --> 01:12:00,608
Did you get hurt?

1718
01:12:00,609 --> 01:12:02,608
I think her skin got rubbed raw...

1719
01:12:02,609 --> 01:12:04,908
- Yes?
- while she was on the floor.

1720
01:12:04,909 --> 01:12:05,919
I think so too.

1721
01:12:05,979 --> 01:12:09,089
I scraped my elbow but only noticed after getting off stage.

1722
01:12:09,219 --> 01:12:10,689
When I went down on the floor.

1723
01:12:10,919 --> 01:12:12,519
It was probably during "She Got It."

1724
01:12:13,019 --> 01:12:14,358
I think I hurt myself there.

1725
01:12:14,359 --> 01:12:16,628
I'm okay. It doesn't hurt that much.

1726
01:12:16,629 --> 01:12:18,059
(As expected, My Star is a pro.)

1727
01:12:18,129 --> 01:12:21,129
Does it take long to prepare for the Waterbomb?

1728
01:12:22,169 --> 01:12:23,569
- The Waterbomb?
- Yes.

1729
01:12:23,869 --> 01:12:26,068
It's not a solo concert, is it?

1730
01:12:26,069 --> 01:12:27,498
- No, it's not.
- Right?

1731
01:12:27,499 --> 01:12:29,838
But do you still prepare for a long time?

1732
01:12:29,839 --> 01:12:32,408
I didn't spend all my time preparing just for this,

1733
01:12:32,409 --> 01:12:34,338
but I did little by little for a while,

1734
01:12:34,339 --> 01:12:36,179
starting about 2 or 3 months ago.

1735
01:12:36,479 --> 01:12:37,648
Is that so?

1736
01:12:37,649 --> 01:12:39,209
(Prepared the performance for 3 months)

1737
01:12:40,379 --> 01:12:42,388
(For the 30-minute performance, )

1738
01:12:42,389 --> 01:12:46,389
(practiced for months)

1739
01:12:46,559 --> 01:12:48,489
- The songs...
- Yes?

1740
01:12:49,059 --> 01:12:50,288
You sing your famous songs...

1741
01:12:50,289 --> 01:12:51,628
- every year.
- I do.

1742
01:12:51,629 --> 01:12:52,958
Do you need to prepare for it?

1743
01:12:52,959 --> 01:12:53,959
Can't you use the old choreography?

1744
01:12:53,960 --> 01:12:55,498
That? You see...

1745
01:12:55,499 --> 01:12:57,128
The song was remixed,

1746
01:12:57,129 --> 01:12:58,498
so even the choreography...

1747
01:12:58,499 --> 01:12:59,868
- So it was a remix.
- was renewed.

1748
01:12:59,869 --> 01:13:00,869
That's right.

1749
01:13:01,399 --> 01:13:03,868
I put a little more effort into preparing for this performance...

1750
01:13:03,869 --> 01:13:05,509
as if it were my last one.

1751
01:13:06,479 --> 01:13:07,838
- Now...
- No more Waterbombs?

1752
01:13:07,839 --> 01:13:10,679
Waterbomb... It's just that...

1753
01:13:10,909 --> 01:13:12,848
I don't know if I can do it again.

1754
01:13:12,849 --> 01:13:15,219
Losing weight is tough.

1755
01:13:15,619 --> 01:13:17,849
Do you have to lose weight?

1756
01:13:18,389 --> 01:13:20,689
If I don't, I become a total pig.

1757
01:13:21,319 --> 01:13:22,529
That's cute.

1758
01:13:23,659 --> 01:13:26,328
As half of the audience is foreigners...

1759
01:13:26,329 --> 01:13:27,458
It might work on them.

1760
01:13:27,459 --> 01:13:30,099
- They might prefer that.
- True.

1761
01:13:30,599 --> 01:13:33,469
(Set to be unleashed at the after-party)

1762
01:13:33,969 --> 01:13:35,439
Are you an only child?

1763
01:13:35,839 --> 01:13:37,109
- No.
- No?

1764
01:13:37,469 --> 01:13:39,579
But I don't get along with my siblings.

1765
01:13:40,079 --> 01:13:41,779
Is that so? I guess you don't click.

1766
01:13:42,879 --> 01:13:45,009
(Laughing brightly at his friend's family situation)

1767
01:13:45,149 --> 01:13:47,119
There's this niece who I really adore.

1768
01:13:47,279 --> 01:13:48,478
- Niece?
- Yes.

1769
01:13:48,479 --> 01:13:49,649
I only see her.

1770
01:13:49,719 --> 01:13:51,218
(Smiling at the thought of his niece)

1771
01:13:51,219 --> 01:13:52,819
How old is she? Is she a baby?

1772
01:13:53,319 --> 01:13:54,658
She was born in 2003.

1773
01:13:54,659 --> 01:13:55,889
She's an adult.

1774
01:13:56,029 --> 01:13:58,928
She graduated from college last year and is now living in New York.

1775
01:13:58,929 --> 01:14:00,098
(Seo Jin's niece lives in New York.)

1776
01:14:00,099 --> 01:14:02,928
- New York?
- My niece also thinks...

1777
01:14:02,929 --> 01:14:04,429
New York is the best city.

1778
01:14:04,699 --> 01:14:06,069
"If it isn't New York, I can't."

1779
01:14:06,339 --> 01:14:08,099
I love Mapo-gu.

1780
01:14:09,209 --> 01:14:12,309
I moved to Mapo-gu, and I'm loving it.

1781
01:14:12,809 --> 01:14:14,239
Aren't you moving to Mapo-gu soon?

1782
01:14:14,379 --> 01:14:16,408
- What?
- Aren't you moving to Mapo-gu?

1783
01:14:16,409 --> 01:14:19,748
I thought so too, but the address turned out to be Seodaemun-gu.

1784
01:14:19,749 --> 01:14:21,448
- Seodaemun-gu.
- Seodaemun-gu.

1785
01:14:21,449 --> 01:14:22,748
Seodaemun-gu is nice too.

1786
01:14:22,749 --> 01:14:24,019
(Not great at geography)

1787
01:14:24,189 --> 01:14:26,759
Isn't Seochon in Seodaemun-gu?

1788
01:14:26,989 --> 01:14:28,588
- No.
- No?

1789
01:14:28,589 --> 01:14:30,358
- Is that in Jongno-gu?
- That's Jongno-gu.

1790
01:14:30,359 --> 01:14:31,788
- I'm sorry.
- You mean like Bukchon and Seochon?

1791
01:14:31,789 --> 01:14:33,298
Yes, Bukchon and Seochon.

1792
01:14:33,299 --> 01:14:35,268
- Seochon.
- Yeonhui-dong is in Seodaemun-gu.

1793
01:14:35,269 --> 01:14:37,469
- Is Yeonhui-dong in Seodaemun-gu?
- Seodaemun-gu is...

1794
01:14:37,499 --> 01:14:39,139
Isn't Sinchon in Seodaemun-gu?

1795
01:14:39,399 --> 01:14:42,669
No. Sinchon is in Mapo-gu.

1796
01:14:43,009 --> 01:14:45,308
No, Hongdae is in...

1797
01:14:45,309 --> 01:14:47,339
- Hongdae is in Mapo-gu.
- Mapo-gu..

1798
01:14:47,609 --> 01:14:49,009
Sinchon is in Seodaemun-gu.

1799
01:14:49,249 --> 01:14:50,449
- Is that so?
- Let's bet.

1800
01:14:50,549 --> 01:14:52,278
- Let's bet.
- How much?

1801
01:14:52,279 --> 01:14:53,648
Okay, I'm in.

1802
01:14:53,649 --> 01:14:54,948
What's your say, BIBI?

1803
01:14:54,949 --> 01:14:56,718
- Sinchon...
- I say Mapo-gu.

1804
01:14:56,719 --> 01:14:57,918
Same here.

1805
01:14:57,919 --> 01:14:59,219
Got it.

1806
01:14:59,359 --> 01:15:00,489
If I win,

1807
01:15:00,889 --> 01:15:02,728
- you give me 50 dollars each.
- Okay.

1808
01:15:02,729 --> 01:15:04,058
If I lose,

1809
01:15:04,059 --> 01:15:05,659
- I'll give you each 50 dollars.
- Okay.

1810
01:15:06,499 --> 01:15:08,058
(Searching right away)

1811
01:15:08,059 --> 01:15:09,069
Okay.

1812
01:15:10,129 --> 01:15:11,629
(Gasping)

1813
01:15:12,499 --> 01:15:15,369
Yonsei-ro, Seodaemun-gu. Okay, 50 dollars each.

1814
01:15:15,969 --> 01:15:18,109
- For real?
- It's in Seodaemun-gu.

1815
01:15:18,839 --> 01:15:20,308
- What?
- Sinchon is in Seodaemun-gu?

1816
01:15:20,309 --> 01:15:22,708
Sinchon is right next to Mapo-gu, but it's in Seodaemun-gu.

1817
01:15:22,709 --> 01:15:25,879
- Really?
- May I wire you the money?

1818
01:15:26,119 --> 01:15:27,949
(Yes, 100 dollars!)

1819
01:15:28,149 --> 01:15:29,688
Is Ahyeon-dong also in Seodaemun-gu?

1820
01:15:29,689 --> 01:15:31,449
Ahyeon-dong is in Seodaemun-gu.

1821
01:15:31,819 --> 01:15:34,289
(Seo Genie is a genius at geography.)

1822
01:15:34,489 --> 01:15:36,258
But how do you know all of that?

1823
01:15:36,259 --> 01:15:39,099
Don't people usually only know about their neighborhood?

1824
01:15:40,499 --> 01:15:42,368
- You know, Yeonhui-dong...
- Yes?

1825
01:15:42,369 --> 01:15:45,969
Two presidents were from that area.

1826
01:15:47,169 --> 01:15:48,889
So it's been a famous area for a long time.

1827
01:15:49,409 --> 01:15:50,808
People were all about Yeonhui-dong.

1828
01:15:50,809 --> 01:15:54,108
Yonsei University used to be Yonhee College.

1829
01:15:54,109 --> 01:15:55,778
Yonhee-Severance, right?

1830
01:15:55,779 --> 01:15:57,809
It's now Yonsei University,

1831
01:15:58,009 --> 01:15:59,929
but it was originally founded as Yonhee College.

1832
01:16:00,379 --> 01:16:02,019
Why did it change to Yonsei University?

1833
01:16:02,919 --> 01:16:04,559
- That's none of my business.
- Yonhee...

1834
01:16:04,819 --> 01:16:07,119
(Confident even when he has no idea)

1835
01:16:07,159 --> 01:16:10,529
I think "Yonsei" is short for "Yonhee-Severance."

1836
01:16:10,759 --> 01:16:12,129
- Really?
- Yes.

1837
01:16:12,359 --> 01:16:13,599
That may make sense.

1838
01:16:13,799 --> 01:16:15,298
No, it's a fact.

1839
01:16:15,299 --> 01:16:16,599
- Is it?
- Yes.

1840
01:16:19,239 --> 01:16:21,168
- Inha University.
- Yes?

1841
01:16:21,169 --> 01:16:23,569
Did you also know it's short for Incheon Hawaii University?

1842
01:16:23,709 --> 01:16:24,968
- Incheon Hawaii?
- Yes.

1843
01:16:24,969 --> 01:16:26,038
- Really?
- Inha University...

1844
01:16:26,039 --> 01:16:27,438
is short for Incheon Hawaii University.

1845
01:16:27,439 --> 01:16:28,479
Are you serious?

1846
01:16:28,579 --> 01:16:30,278
You just came up with it, didn't you?

1847
01:16:30,279 --> 01:16:32,418
- No, it's true.
- That's absurd.

1848
01:16:32,419 --> 01:16:33,578
I've never heard of that before.

1849
01:16:33,579 --> 01:16:36,248
Really, Inha University is short for Incheon Hawaii University.

1850
01:16:36,249 --> 01:16:37,748
- Come on.
- It's true!

1851
01:16:37,749 --> 01:16:39,018
- No way.
- Come on.

1852
01:16:39,019 --> 01:16:42,158
Inha University has no other founding name.

1853
01:16:42,159 --> 01:16:43,388
It's simply Inha University.

1854
01:16:43,389 --> 01:16:44,389
- Hawaii isn't part of it.
- How much...

1855
01:16:44,390 --> 01:16:45,598
How much do you want to bet? Fifty dollars?

1856
01:16:45,599 --> 01:16:46,658
A return bet?

1857
01:16:46,659 --> 01:16:48,129
- A return bet.
- Good.

1858
01:16:48,499 --> 01:16:50,768
I might just walk away with...

1859
01:16:50,769 --> 01:16:52,568
fifteen dollars by accident.

1860
01:16:52,569 --> 01:16:53,569
(Does "Inha" stand for "Incheon Hawaii University?")

1861
01:16:53,569 --> 01:16:54,569
Inha University.

1862
01:16:54,570 --> 01:16:56,009
(Searching Inha University)

1863
01:16:56,939 --> 01:16:57,939
I'm right.

1864
01:16:57,940 --> 01:17:00,178
"The name 'Inha' of Inha University comes from..."

1865
01:17:00,179 --> 01:17:02,808
"the first syllable of Incheon and the first syllable of Hawaii."

1866
01:17:02,809 --> 01:17:05,778
"Inha University was founded in Incheon in 1954 with donations..."

1867
01:17:05,779 --> 01:17:06,978
"from Korean immigrants in Hawaii,"

1868
01:17:06,979 --> 01:17:08,478
"commemorating the 50th anniversary of Korean immigration..."

1869
01:17:08,479 --> 01:17:09,518
"and supporting..."

1870
01:17:09,519 --> 01:17:10,548
- "Korea's industrial development." - Listen.

1871
01:17:10,549 --> 01:17:12,318
That was how it was founded, and it was named Inha University...

1872
01:17:12,319 --> 01:17:14,619
- Is that so?
- from the start.

1873
01:17:15,219 --> 01:17:18,488
It didn't have a founding name of Incheon Hawaii University.

1874
01:17:18,489 --> 01:17:19,658
Come on.

1875
01:17:19,659 --> 01:17:21,539
- Incheon...
- That's basically the same thing.

1876
01:17:21,929 --> 01:17:23,728
The name is from...

1877
01:17:23,729 --> 01:17:26,299
the first syllables of Incheon and Hawaii, so she's right.

1878
01:17:26,569 --> 01:17:29,509
(Pouting out of fluster)

1879
01:17:30,239 --> 01:17:31,269
Give it back.

1880
01:17:31,509 --> 01:17:33,179
- Give it back!
- Give it back.

1881
01:17:34,039 --> 01:17:37,248
Inha University started off as Inha Engineering College.

1882
01:17:37,249 --> 01:17:39,729
- Seriously, how annoying.
- Either way, no Incheon or Hawaii.

1883
01:17:40,449 --> 01:17:42,118
- Guess what Ajou University is.
- What?

1884
01:17:42,119 --> 01:17:43,388
Guess what Ajou University is.

1885
01:17:43,389 --> 01:17:46,858
Ajou...

1886
01:17:46,859 --> 01:17:48,689
It stands for "Asia State University."

1887
01:17:49,389 --> 01:17:50,828
- For real?
- Yes.

1888
01:17:50,829 --> 01:17:52,898
Do you want to lose all your fortune?

1889
01:17:52,899 --> 01:17:54,498
No, it's true.

1890
01:17:54,499 --> 01:17:55,698
- It's all written here.
- Do you want to lose...

1891
01:17:55,699 --> 01:17:56,898
all your fortune?

1892
01:17:56,899 --> 01:17:58,869
- It's all on here.
- Really.

1893
01:17:59,299 --> 01:18:00,938
Here, if you search up Asia State University...

1894
01:18:00,939 --> 01:18:03,209
It was founded as Ajou Technical Junior College...

1895
01:18:03,369 --> 01:18:05,008
- Really, how annoying.
- and later became Ajou University.

1896
01:18:05,009 --> 01:18:06,778
- You're a handful.
- I found nothing about it...

1897
01:18:06,779 --> 01:18:08,508
being called Asia State University.

1898
01:18:08,509 --> 01:18:11,509
I'm only reading Wikipedia.

1899
01:18:12,149 --> 01:18:13,718
Wikipedia.

1900
01:18:13,719 --> 01:18:15,748
Anyone can write on it.

1901
01:18:15,749 --> 01:18:17,618
You shouldn't trust it.

1902
01:18:17,619 --> 01:18:20,389
With Inha and Ajou, you owe me 150 dollars.

1903
01:18:20,619 --> 01:18:23,358
Come on, I'm right. Stop being stubborn.

1904
01:18:23,359 --> 01:18:25,929
Yes, just say that she's right.

1905
01:18:27,259 --> 01:18:30,028
- Seo Jin, you're a little...
- Yes?

1906
01:18:30,029 --> 01:18:32,399
I don't know how to put it into words,

1907
01:18:32,539 --> 01:18:34,998
but you're hateful, very hateful.

1908
01:18:34,999 --> 01:18:36,209
I hear that a lot.

1909
01:18:36,509 --> 01:18:38,439
- You do?
- Gosh.

1910
01:18:38,639 --> 01:18:40,009
How hateful.

1911
01:18:40,439 --> 01:18:42,378
Either way, you owe me 50 dollars.

1912
01:18:42,379 --> 01:18:44,749
Can I get a cash receipt?

1913
01:18:44,849 --> 01:18:46,019
Of course not.

1914
01:18:46,079 --> 01:18:47,978
(BIBI may have lost money, )

1915
01:18:47,979 --> 01:18:50,688
- We're in the hot Yeonnam-dong.
- Yeonnam-dong.

1916
01:18:50,689 --> 01:18:52,209
(but she's getting close to her food!)

1917
01:18:52,319 --> 01:18:53,458
It looks good.

1918
01:18:53,459 --> 01:18:54,518
(My Star's Schedule:)

1919
01:18:54,519 --> 01:18:56,735
(7:05pm, BIBI's Yeonnam-dong regular spot for an after-party)

1920
01:18:56,759 --> 01:18:59,028
(The food has been delivered.)

1921
01:18:59,029 --> 01:19:00,159
(Received by Lee Seo Jin)

1922
01:19:01,829 --> 01:19:04,728
(Reuniting with spicy chicken feet after 2 weeks)

1923
01:19:04,729 --> 01:19:05,869
Hi.

1924
01:19:05,939 --> 01:19:07,169
Oh, my gosh.

1925
01:19:07,339 --> 01:19:09,208
What... Look around.

1926
01:19:09,209 --> 01:19:10,738
I'm going to dig in first. I'm starving.

1927
01:19:10,739 --> 01:19:12,639
Go ahead. Dig in.

1928
01:19:12,739 --> 01:19:14,479
(Frantically moving hands)

1929
01:19:15,179 --> 01:19:17,308
(Overjoyed to finally meet her favorite food)

1930
01:19:17,309 --> 01:19:18,309
(Opening)

1931
01:19:19,549 --> 01:19:20,879
What is that? Tteokbokki?

1932
01:19:20,919 --> 01:19:22,419
- No, chicken feet.
- Chicken feet.

1933
01:19:23,719 --> 01:19:27,419
(My Star's mind was filled with thoughts of chicken feet.)

1934
01:19:29,489 --> 01:19:32,129
(Finally tasting the earthly indulgence after 2 weeks)

1935
01:19:32,229 --> 01:19:33,658
Could we get more plates?

1936
01:19:33,659 --> 01:19:34,958
- Sure.
- A big plate.

1937
01:19:34,959 --> 01:19:36,469
(Uneasy)

1938
01:19:36,929 --> 01:19:38,569
I'm... Thank you for the food.

1939
01:19:38,669 --> 01:19:40,868
- Dig in.
- Okay.

1940
01:19:40,869 --> 01:19:44,509
(It's finally time to taste the long-awaited chicken feet.)

1941
01:19:45,169 --> 01:19:46,209
(Amazed)

1942
01:19:48,009 --> 01:19:49,608
The last time I had something saucy...

1943
01:19:49,609 --> 01:19:50,678
It's been a while, right?

1944
01:19:50,679 --> 01:19:51,978
Was about two weeks ago.

1945
01:19:51,979 --> 01:19:53,019
Goodness.

1946
01:19:56,549 --> 01:19:58,689
(It's delicious!)

1947
01:19:59,289 --> 01:20:00,759
I'll pour out the juice.

1948
01:20:02,589 --> 01:20:04,828
(My Star's reward for 2 weeks of patience)

1949
01:20:04,829 --> 01:20:06,898
- For two weeks.
- You also ate chicken breasts.

1950
01:20:06,899 --> 01:20:09,568
Chicken breasts and soymilk noodles.

1951
01:20:09,569 --> 01:20:10,868
I'm really looking forward...

1952
01:20:10,869 --> 01:20:13,569
to eating dinner after it all ends. It's exciting.

1953
01:20:13,969 --> 01:20:15,139
That looks good.

1954
01:20:15,399 --> 01:20:17,769
My energy is really low.

1955
01:20:18,369 --> 01:20:20,289
Yes. My energy is really low because I'm hungry.

1956
01:20:21,109 --> 01:20:23,079
She must be really hungry.

1957
01:20:23,309 --> 01:20:25,109
(In bliss)

1958
01:20:25,949 --> 01:20:27,619
(Eating the beef intestine)

1959
01:20:29,589 --> 01:20:32,119
(It's so good that she can't help but dance.)

1960
01:20:33,089 --> 01:20:34,089
(Staring)

1961
01:20:34,090 --> 01:20:36,228
You must want rice. Are you okay?

1962
01:20:36,229 --> 01:20:37,289
I'm okay.

1963
01:20:37,789 --> 01:20:39,358
Should I have ordered some rice?

1964
01:20:39,359 --> 01:20:40,398
(They want her to enjoy it to the fullest today.)

1965
01:20:40,399 --> 01:20:41,429
It's okay.

1966
01:20:42,529 --> 01:20:44,329
Eat slowly.

1967
01:20:44,669 --> 01:20:45,969
Have it with that.

1968
01:20:46,539 --> 01:20:47,738
- It's spicy.
- Okay.

1969
01:20:47,739 --> 01:20:49,008
(Finally trying some food)

1970
01:20:49,009 --> 01:20:50,639
Try it.

1971
01:20:51,709 --> 01:20:53,209
- It's boneless, right?
- Yes.

1972
01:20:53,879 --> 01:20:56,179
- Is this the beef intestine?
- Yes.

1973
01:20:58,479 --> 01:21:00,578
- I love offal.
- What?

1974
01:21:00,579 --> 01:21:01,779
Offal.

1975
01:21:02,149 --> 01:21:03,719
Offal. You know, innards.

1976
01:21:04,189 --> 01:21:05,819
I'm not a fan of offal.

1977
01:21:06,359 --> 01:21:07,618
You can't eat it at all.

1978
01:21:07,619 --> 01:21:10,728
I used to be something like a vegetarian in the past.

1979
01:21:10,729 --> 01:21:12,698
- Really?
- Slightly, yes.

1980
01:21:12,699 --> 01:21:13,858
- I...
- He's lying.

1981
01:21:13,859 --> 01:21:15,058
(Nonsense)

1982
01:21:15,059 --> 01:21:16,798
- Stop lying.
- No, for real.

1983
01:21:16,799 --> 01:21:18,668
I couldn't eat meat at all.

1984
01:21:18,669 --> 01:21:20,189
(Kwang Kyu was far from a meat lover.)

1985
01:21:21,299 --> 01:21:23,238
The fact that you were a vegetarian is a shocker.

1986
01:21:23,239 --> 01:21:24,469
He's lying.

1987
01:21:24,709 --> 01:21:26,078
It's a lie, okay?

1988
01:21:26,079 --> 01:21:27,909
He digs into pork belly like mad.

1989
01:21:28,339 --> 01:21:31,209
(The white lies are back.)

1990
01:21:32,519 --> 01:21:33,519
I'm full.

1991
01:21:35,249 --> 01:21:36,548
- Full?
- You barely touched it.

1992
01:21:36,549 --> 01:21:38,719
She's full after barely touching the food.

1993
01:21:39,989 --> 01:21:41,888
- Do you need napkins?
- Thank you.

1994
01:21:41,889 --> 01:21:43,259
(Taking care of her in between)

1995
01:21:44,429 --> 01:21:46,899
I'll wire you the money once you give me your number.

1996
01:21:47,559 --> 01:21:48,598
Don't worry about it.

1997
01:21:48,599 --> 01:21:50,699
(A full stomach brings back the bet from the car)

1998
01:21:51,069 --> 01:21:52,169
How much will you send me?

1999
01:21:53,199 --> 01:21:54,499
Fifty dollars.

2000
01:21:54,969 --> 01:21:56,468
Are you just ignoring the other two?

2001
01:21:56,469 --> 01:21:59,108
I'm not. I stated the facts, okay?

2002
01:21:59,109 --> 01:22:00,478
(A little scared)

2003
01:22:00,479 --> 01:22:02,949
It's actually Incheon Hawaii University!

2004
01:22:05,719 --> 01:22:06,819
You know.

2005
01:22:07,449 --> 01:22:09,019
This feels like a fight with a kid.

2006
01:22:10,189 --> 01:22:11,249
I get it.

2007
01:22:11,389 --> 01:22:14,489
Give me a minute. Let me ask my cousin.

2008
01:22:14,589 --> 01:22:16,428
- Call your cousin.
- I'll call her.

2009
01:22:16,429 --> 01:22:17,928
- Did she attend that school?
- Yes.

2010
01:22:17,929 --> 01:22:20,029
- Which school? Inha University?
- Yes.

2011
01:22:20,259 --> 01:22:22,998
I'm sure I have a friend who graduated from Inha University.

2012
01:22:22,999 --> 01:22:24,639
- Inha University...
- There's Kim Gu Ra.

2013
01:22:25,799 --> 01:22:27,098
Ask Kim Gu Ra.

2014
01:22:27,099 --> 01:22:28,579
(Calling in all possible connections)

2015
01:22:28,639 --> 01:22:30,468
- Hey.
- What's up?

2016
01:22:30,469 --> 01:22:32,708
I explained that Inha University stands for...

2017
01:22:32,709 --> 01:22:35,309
"Incheon Hawaii University," but no one believed me.

2018
01:22:35,698 --> 01:22:37,428
- But you're right.
- Right?

2019
01:22:37,658 --> 01:22:38,927
(She's right?)

2020
01:22:38,928 --> 01:22:41,498
I entered Inha University in 2016.

2021
01:22:41,668 --> 01:22:44,038
Inha University does stand for "Incheon Hawaii University."

2022
01:22:44,568 --> 01:22:48,207
(The Inha University graduate sets the record straight.)

2023
01:22:48,208 --> 01:22:51,377
- These people are driving me crazy.
- Is everything okay now?

2024
01:22:51,378 --> 01:22:52,748
(Laughing)

2025
01:22:53,008 --> 01:22:55,348
They kept saying I was wrong.

2026
01:22:55,948 --> 01:22:57,277
You got it right.

2027
01:22:57,278 --> 01:22:59,787
- Right? Thanks.
- No problem.

2028
01:22:59,788 --> 01:23:01,647
- Bye.
- Thanks.

2029
01:23:01,648 --> 01:23:02,808
(My Star is back to smiling.)

2030
01:23:02,988 --> 01:23:04,118
(I was right, wasn't I?)

2031
01:23:05,058 --> 01:23:07,557
- Right. Even a graduate said so.
- Listen.

2032
01:23:07,558 --> 01:23:10,228
I'll accept it if even Kim Gu Ra says it's true.

2033
01:23:10,458 --> 01:23:12,398
(You want another phone call?)

2034
01:23:12,868 --> 01:23:14,868
If another graduate says it's true,

2035
01:23:15,568 --> 01:23:16,767
I'll accept it.

2036
01:23:16,768 --> 01:23:17,967
(Extremely childish)

2037
01:23:17,968 --> 01:23:19,467
Our conversations today...

2038
01:23:19,468 --> 01:23:21,807
should be about the Waterbomb or BIBI...

2039
01:23:21,808 --> 01:23:23,307
Can't you just check with him?

2040
01:23:23,308 --> 01:23:24,578
- Hurry up.
- Please.

2041
01:23:24,638 --> 01:23:26,307
(Most curious about the truth behind Inha University)

2042
01:23:26,308 --> 01:23:27,347
- Hurry up and call him.
- Please.

2043
01:23:27,348 --> 01:23:28,548
Fine. Goodness.

2044
01:23:30,948 --> 01:23:32,187
- Hello?
- Hey.

2045
01:23:32,188 --> 01:23:34,047
- Are you busy?
- No, it's fine.

2046
01:23:34,048 --> 01:23:35,787
- Are you free for a call?
- Yes.

2047
01:23:35,788 --> 01:23:36,788
Listen.

2048
01:23:36,789 --> 01:23:38,287
You graduated from Inha University, right?

2049
01:23:38,288 --> 01:23:39,688
Yes, I did.

2050
01:23:39,958 --> 01:23:43,158
Does Inha University stand for Incheon Hawaii University?

2051
01:23:44,498 --> 01:23:46,527
Does it stand for Incheon Hawaii University?

2052
01:23:46,528 --> 01:23:47,567
It does.

2053
01:23:47,568 --> 01:23:48,837
- It does?
- Yes.

2054
01:23:48,838 --> 01:23:49,867
It does.

2055
01:23:49,868 --> 01:23:51,537
(My Star was right!)

2056
01:23:51,538 --> 01:23:53,007
- Seriously?
- As far as I know,

2057
01:23:53,008 --> 01:23:54,708
- it started in the 1950s...
- Yes?

2058
01:23:54,868 --> 01:23:58,507
With donations from first-generation Korean immigrants...

2059
01:23:58,508 --> 01:24:01,548
from Hawaii who were living in Incheon...

2060
01:24:01,578 --> 01:24:03,818
at the time. Why the question?

2061
01:24:04,818 --> 01:24:06,647
- So the name...
- Incheon Hawaii,

2062
01:24:06,648 --> 01:24:08,088
hence Inha.

2063
01:24:09,288 --> 01:24:11,927
Incheon Hawaii, hence Inha University.

2064
01:24:11,928 --> 01:24:12,957
Correct.

2065
01:24:12,958 --> 01:24:15,197
That's how you know it as, right?

2066
01:24:15,198 --> 01:24:16,658
No, it's the truth.

2067
01:24:17,298 --> 01:24:19,097
(Feeling much better)

2068
01:24:19,098 --> 01:24:21,097
We're in the middle of shooting My Genie Secretary.

2069
01:24:21,098 --> 01:24:22,867
- Thank you, Gu Ra.
- No worries.

2070
01:24:22,868 --> 01:24:24,537
Thank you very much.

2071
01:24:24,538 --> 01:24:26,637
It's basic knowledge, you know?

2072
01:24:26,638 --> 01:24:29,008
(It's basic knowledge, you know?)

2073
01:24:29,138 --> 01:24:31,007
Because we wouldn't believe her,

2074
01:24:31,008 --> 01:24:32,947
it was only right for her to be infuriated.

2075
01:24:32,948 --> 01:24:34,047
Inha University...

2076
01:24:34,048 --> 01:24:35,977
stands for Incheon Hawaii University?

2077
01:24:35,978 --> 01:24:38,348
I never knew.

2078
01:24:40,488 --> 01:24:41,748
What about Ajou University?

2079
01:24:41,958 --> 01:24:43,687
- Who do we ask?
- Asia State University?

2080
01:24:43,688 --> 01:24:45,227
I know someone who graduated from Ajou University.

2081
01:24:45,228 --> 01:24:46,687
Jee Seok Jin graduated from Ajou University.

2082
01:24:46,688 --> 01:24:48,204
- Is that so?
- He graduated from Ajou University.

2083
01:24:48,228 --> 01:24:50,297
How do you know everyone's university?

2084
01:24:50,298 --> 01:24:51,457
He mentioned it the last time...

2085
01:24:51,458 --> 01:24:52,628
- we were shooting.
- Did he?

2086
01:24:54,998 --> 01:24:56,698
- Hello?
- Seok Jin.

2087
01:24:57,298 --> 01:24:58,837
- Pardon?
- Seok Jin?

2088
01:24:58,838 --> 01:25:00,237
- He said, "Pardon?" - Who is this?

2089
01:25:00,238 --> 01:25:01,938
(Puzzled)

2090
01:25:03,950 --> 01:25:05,790
- Hello?
- Seok Jin.

2091
01:25:06,260 --> 01:25:07,759
- Pardon?
- Seok Jin?

2092
01:25:07,760 --> 01:25:09,329
- He said, "Pardon?" - Who is this?

2093
01:25:09,330 --> 01:25:10,890
(Puzzled)

2094
01:25:11,560 --> 01:25:13,030
It's me, Kwang Kyu.

2095
01:25:13,330 --> 01:25:14,460
Hey.

2096
01:25:14,860 --> 01:25:16,430
I lost your phone number.

2097
01:25:17,700 --> 01:25:18,839
(Phone numbers expose their true level of closeness)

2098
01:25:18,840 --> 01:25:19,900
What's up?

2099
01:25:20,970 --> 01:25:22,109
- I've got a question for you.
- Kwang Kyu.

2100
01:25:22,110 --> 01:25:23,790
You graduated from Ajou University, right?

2101
01:25:23,910 --> 01:25:24,969
Yes.

2102
01:25:24,970 --> 01:25:28,209
I want to know something about Ajou University.

2103
01:25:28,210 --> 01:25:29,650
What show is this for?

2104
01:25:30,580 --> 01:25:32,480
My Genie Secretary.

2105
01:25:33,280 --> 01:25:34,579
It's going on again?

2106
01:25:34,580 --> 01:25:35,620
Yes.

2107
01:25:35,890 --> 01:25:37,250
Congratulations.

2108
01:25:37,350 --> 01:25:38,620
Hi, Seok Jin.

2109
01:25:39,090 --> 01:25:41,219
- Hey, who is this?
- It's Seo Jin.

2110
01:25:41,220 --> 01:25:43,629
Hi, Seo Jin.

2111
01:25:43,630 --> 01:25:45,460
- Our Celebrity Lee.
- Hi.

2112
01:25:45,930 --> 01:25:46,959
You see,

2113
01:25:46,960 --> 01:25:48,669
- we're having...
- Ajou University?

2114
01:25:48,670 --> 01:25:50,270
A little dispute about Ajou University.

2115
01:25:50,330 --> 01:25:51,939
What about it? What about Ajou University?

2116
01:25:51,940 --> 01:25:53,800
BIBI is our guest.

2117
01:25:54,100 --> 01:25:56,270
- She said Ajou University...
- Yes?

2118
01:25:56,440 --> 01:26:00,010
Stands for Asia State University.

2119
01:26:01,080 --> 01:26:04,380
We kept telling her that it was nonsense.

2120
01:26:04,750 --> 01:26:06,050
Ultimately,

2121
01:26:06,120 --> 01:26:09,790
you came to mind as you graduated from Ajou University.

2122
01:26:09,990 --> 01:26:12,119
We joked around with people who didn't know,

2123
01:26:12,120 --> 01:26:13,289
saying it was Asia State University.

2124
01:26:13,290 --> 01:26:14,459
(We joked around.)

2125
01:26:14,460 --> 01:26:15,529
We joked around.

2126
01:26:15,530 --> 01:26:17,559
(Frozen in place)

2127
01:26:17,560 --> 01:26:18,859
Was it a joke?

2128
01:26:18,860 --> 01:26:20,300
You're joking, right?

2129
01:26:21,100 --> 01:26:23,500
We joked around, saying it was Asia State University.

2130
01:26:23,770 --> 01:26:25,640
(Laughing brightly)

2131
01:26:25,740 --> 01:26:27,299
- Thank you.
- No problem.

2132
01:26:27,300 --> 01:26:28,639
I'll call you again.

2133
01:26:28,640 --> 01:26:31,310
- Hi, BIBI.
- Hi.

2134
01:26:31,340 --> 01:26:32,780
Kwang Kyu.

2135
01:26:32,810 --> 01:26:33,940
Yes?

2136
01:26:34,140 --> 01:26:36,010
- Don't treat me like...
- Yes?

2137
01:26:36,110 --> 01:26:38,349
I'm older in a public setting.

2138
01:26:38,350 --> 01:26:40,430
(Don't treat me like I'm older in a public setting.)

2139
01:26:41,720 --> 01:26:42,820
Sir.

2140
01:26:43,220 --> 01:26:45,589
Congratulations on turning 60, sir.

2141
01:26:45,590 --> 01:26:47,419
- Take care.
- Congratulations.

2142
01:26:47,420 --> 01:26:48,530
Thanks.

2143
01:26:48,660 --> 01:26:51,090
- Thank you, sir.
- Bye.

2144
01:26:51,460 --> 01:26:54,030
(Feeling bad for some reason)

2145
01:26:54,230 --> 01:26:55,699
Food has made me...

2146
01:26:55,700 --> 01:26:56,799
- Sleepy?
- You're sleepy, right?

2147
01:26:56,800 --> 01:26:58,569
- sleepy.
- Of course.

2148
01:26:58,570 --> 01:27:00,569
- Remember how I had Homerun Ball?
- Yes.

2149
01:27:00,570 --> 01:27:03,870
My blood sugar level has spiked.

2150
01:27:04,070 --> 01:27:06,409
Did you go on a diet for two weeks...

2151
01:27:06,410 --> 01:27:08,379
- for today's Waterbomb?
- Yes.

2152
01:27:08,380 --> 01:27:09,550
Two weeks?

2153
01:27:09,780 --> 01:27:12,219
- Yes.
- Just for this one very day?

2154
01:27:12,220 --> 01:27:13,680
Amazing.

2155
01:27:14,650 --> 01:27:17,049
I asked my company to book me...

2156
01:27:17,050 --> 01:27:20,359
for the Waterbomb Festival to sing...

2157
01:27:20,360 --> 01:27:23,629
- "Open Sesame." - You asked for too much.

2158
01:27:23,630 --> 01:27:26,199
I was going to sing it as "Open Waterbomb."

2159
01:27:26,200 --> 01:27:28,259
Don't you think it's better...

2160
01:27:28,260 --> 01:27:30,270
to sing alone in the bathroom?

2161
01:27:31,030 --> 01:27:32,540
After watching it,

2162
01:27:32,570 --> 01:27:34,499
I really want to perform now.

2163
01:27:34,500 --> 01:27:36,140
It was super cool.

2164
01:27:36,410 --> 01:27:39,909
Those who come to the Waterbomb Festival are...

2165
01:27:39,910 --> 01:27:42,710
ready to have some fun.

2166
01:27:42,810 --> 01:27:43,950
(Let's go!)

2167
01:27:44,210 --> 01:27:46,549
They go with the flow,

2168
01:27:46,550 --> 01:27:47,720
matching the energy.

2169
01:27:48,650 --> 01:27:51,720
So as not to disappoint the audience who paid to be there.

2170
01:27:52,520 --> 01:27:54,690
I have to show the audience everything I can.

2171
01:27:54,990 --> 01:27:56,090
Capitalism.

2172
01:27:56,430 --> 01:27:58,700
I'll tell you when you come by my house.

2173
01:27:58,830 --> 01:28:00,329
Can we drop by your house?

2174
01:28:00,330 --> 01:28:01,400
Of course.

2175
01:28:01,860 --> 01:28:04,369
Someone who confidently carves...

2176
01:28:04,370 --> 01:28:06,000
her own path in life.

2177
01:28:07,040 --> 01:28:10,570
Someone who keeps moving in the direction she wants,

2178
01:28:11,140 --> 01:28:12,839
no matter what anyone else says.

2179
01:28:12,840 --> 01:28:14,240
BIBI is like that.

2180
01:28:15,310 --> 01:28:17,009
The queen of "Bam Yang Gang."

2181
01:28:17,010 --> 01:28:21,450
I was so happy to have met my Cinderella today.

2182
01:28:21,550 --> 01:28:24,419
It's such a relief that her performance...

2183
01:28:24,420 --> 01:28:26,119
ended smoothly...

2184
01:28:26,120 --> 01:28:28,220
without any problems.

2185
01:28:29,190 --> 01:28:32,159
The best moment was when Seo Jin...

2186
01:28:32,160 --> 01:28:33,760
wrapped me with a towel.

2187
01:28:34,030 --> 01:28:36,429
It gave me the relief that it was over.

2188
01:28:36,430 --> 01:28:40,000
He was so kind to me, which made me happy.

2189
01:28:41,340 --> 01:28:43,409
Good job, everyone. Thank you for today.

2190
01:28:43,410 --> 01:28:46,240
- Well done, My Star.
- Good job.

2191
01:28:47,080 --> 01:28:49,250
(A surprise visit to My Genie Secretary)

2192
01:28:49,480 --> 01:28:51,610
(My Star Cha Tae Hyun)

2193
01:28:51,980 --> 01:28:54,280
How do I pay my part-time managers?

2194
01:28:54,320 --> 01:28:55,850
- How do I pay you?
- Part-time pay?

2195
01:28:56,250 --> 01:28:58,960
(First paycheck ever in My Genie Secretary?)

2196
01:28:59,090 --> 01:29:01,130
Long-distance trips, late nights, and weekend duty.

2197
01:29:01,160 --> 01:29:02,760
It came to a little over 200 dollars.

2198
01:29:03,190 --> 01:29:05,930
(Give us more.)

2199
01:29:07,200 --> 01:29:08,930
(And so...)

2200
01:29:09,130 --> 01:29:11,930
(Genie will do anything for the paycheck.)

2201
01:29:12,170 --> 01:29:14,640
(From guiding the way around the venue)

2202
01:29:15,470 --> 01:29:18,170
(Serving up a meal enthusiastically)

2203
01:29:18,470 --> 01:29:20,790
(Making sure there's warm barley tea for the sick My Star)

2204
01:29:20,910 --> 01:29:22,079
(Things were going well.)

2205
01:29:22,080 --> 01:29:23,710
(But Kwang Kyu loses focus?)

2206
01:29:24,150 --> 01:29:25,349
Kwang Kyu.

2207
01:29:25,350 --> 01:29:26,950
She's going to catch my cold.

2208
01:29:28,750 --> 01:29:30,290
(I'll set things right!)

2209
01:29:30,490 --> 01:29:31,990
(Sorry, I'll get a grip.)

2210
01:29:32,360 --> 01:29:35,390
(Secure the lost paycheck)

2211
01:29:36,860 --> 01:29:39,160
Ten dollars!

2212
01:29:39,600 --> 01:29:41,100
Isn't he the first to pay us?

2213
01:29:42,530 --> 01:29:44,530
(Capitalism is the best!)

2214
01:29:46,000 --> 01:29:50,410
(And My Star's passion-filled performance)

2215
01:29:53,080 --> 01:29:54,240
(I love you.)

2216
01:29:54,740 --> 01:29:57,780
(A medley of hit songs that gets the crowd singing along)

2217
01:29:57,880 --> 01:30:01,380
(It's the 1st day of My Genie Secretary.)

2218
01:30:02,620 --> 01:30:03,790
It's the first day!

2219
01:30:05,420 --> 01:30:09,090
(My Genie Secretary)
